#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:6
msgid "FindOpenMP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:8
msgid "Finds Open Multi-Processing (OpenMP) support in a compiler:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:10
msgid "find_package(OpenMP [<version>] [COMPONENTS <langs>...] [...])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:14
msgid ""
"If the compiler supports OpenMP, the flags required to compile with OpenMP "
"support are returned in variables for the different languages.  The "
"variables may be empty if the compiler does not need a special flag to "
"support OpenMP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:18
msgid "Clang support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:22
msgid "Components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:24
msgid ""
"This module supports components that can be specified using the standard "
"syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:27
msgid "find_package(OpenMP [COMPONENTS <langs>...])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:31
msgid ""
"Each of these components controls the various languages to search OpenMP "
"support for.  The following components are exposed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:34
msgid "``C``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:37
msgid "``CXX``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:40
msgid "``Fortran``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:43
msgid "``CUDA``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:46
msgid ""
"The ``CUDA`` language component is supported when using a CUDA compiler that "
"supports OpenMP on the host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:49
msgid ""
"If no components are specified, module checks for all of them automatically, "
"depending on the enabled languages in the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:53
msgid "Imported Targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:55
msgid "This module provides the following :ref:`Imported Targets`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:57
msgid "``OpenMP::OpenMP_<lang>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:60
msgid ""
"Target encapsulating the OpenMP usage requirements for language ``<lang>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:62
msgid "``OpenMP::OpenMP_<lang>_Offload``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:65
msgid ""
"Target for code whose OpenMP ``target`` regions may be offloaded to a "
"device, for ``<lang>`` of ``C``, ``CXX``, or ``Fortran``.  It links "
"``OpenMP::OpenMP_<lang>`` and, when offload is enabled with the "
"``OpenMP_<lang>_OFFLOAD`` or ``OpenMP_<lang>_OFFLOAD_FLAGS`` variables, adds "
"the offload flags when compiling ``<lang>`` sources.  It also adds them, "
"together with the OpenMP flags, when the link is done by a compiler with the "
"same :variable:`CMAKE_<LANG>_COMPILER_ID`, because compilers need both in "
"order to link device code.  When offload is not enabled, it is equivalent to "
"``OpenMP::OpenMP_<lang>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:75
msgid ""
"With NVHPC, an executable linked by NVHPC must also link the offload target "
"when it uses a shared library with offloaded code, for example through "
"``$<LINK_ONLY:OpenMP::OpenMP_<lang>_Offload>`` in the library's "
"``INTERFACE`` link libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:80
msgid ""
"Linking through a separate linker, as with Visual Studio generators or "
"``clang-cl``, is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:84
msgid "Input Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:86
msgid "The following variables may be set to influence this module's behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:88
msgid "``OpenMP_RUNTIME_MSVC``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:91
msgid ""
"Specify the `OpenMP Runtime <msvc-openmp_>`_ when compiling with the MSVC "
"compiler (``cl``).  If set to a non-empty value, such as ``experimental`` or "
"``llvm``, it will be passed as the value of the ``-openmp:`` flag.  This has "
"no effect with other compilers, including ``clang-cl``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:99
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_OFFLOAD``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:102
msgid ""
"Enables OpenMP ``target`` offload for targets that link "
"``OpenMP::OpenMP_<lang>_Offload``.  If not defined, offload is enabled when "
"``OpenMP_<lang>_OFFLOAD_FLAGS`` is non-empty.  If defined, its boolean value "
"decides, so ``OFF`` disables offload even when flags are set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:108
msgid ""
"The offload flags are ``OpenMP_<lang>_OFFLOAD_FLAGS`` if non-empty, and "
"otherwise a default for the compiler:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:111
msgid ""
"GNU: none.  GCC offloads to the devices whose offload compilers are "
"installed, such as ``gcc-offload-nvptx`` on Debian and Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:113
msgid "NVHPC: ``-mp=gpu``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:114
msgid ""
"IntelLLVM with a GNU-like command line (``icx``, ``icpx``, ``ifx``): ``-"
"fopenmp-targets=spir64``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:116
msgid ""
"Cray, CrayClang: none.  The device comes from the loaded ``craype-accel-*`` "
"module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:119
msgid ""
"Other compilers, including Clang, have no default.  Enabling offload for "
"them without ``OpenMP_<lang>_OFFLOAD_FLAGS`` is an error, even if the "
"package is ``QUIET`` or the component is optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:123
msgid ""
"Targets linking only ``OpenMP::OpenMP_<lang>`` are not affected. Projects "
"using the result variables must add the device flags for compiling and "
"linking themselves.  Disabling offload only removes what the offload target "
"would add; it does not undo offload enabled by other compiler flags or by "
"the environment.  ``OpenMP_<lang>_FOUND`` and ``OpenMP_<lang>_VERSION`` "
"describe host OpenMP support only; the module does not check that offload "
"works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:131
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_OFFLOAD_FLAGS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:134
msgid ""
"Compiler flags selecting the device(s) to offload OpenMP ``target`` regions "
"to, replacing the compiler's default described above.  For example, ``--"
"offload-arch=sm_80`` for Clang, ``-foffload=nvptx-none`` for GCC, or ``-"
"mp=gpu -gpu=cc80`` for NVHPC.  The value is a command-line string, split "
"into arguments as by the ``SHELL:`` prefix "
"of :command:`target_compile_options`.  An empty or whitespace-only value "
"counts as not set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:143
msgid "Result Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:145
msgid "This module defines the following variables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:147
msgid "``OpenMP_FOUND``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:150
msgid ""
"Boolean indicating that OpenMP flags for all requested languages were "
"found.  If no components are specified, this variable is set to boolean true "
"if OpenMP settings for all enabled languages were detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:154
msgid "``OpenMP_VERSION``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:157
msgid ""
"Minimal version of the OpenMP standard detected among the requested "
"languages, or all enabled languages if no components were specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:160
msgid ""
"This module will set the following variables per language in the project, "
"where ``<lang>`` is one of C, CXX, CUDA, or Fortran:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:163
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_FOUND``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:166
msgid ""
"Boolean indicating whether the (requested version of) OpenMP support for "
"``<lang>`` was detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:169
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_VERSION``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:172
msgid "OpenMP version implemented by the ``<lang>`` compiler, if available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:174
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_VERSION_MAJOR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:177
msgid ""
"Major version of OpenMP implemented by the ``<lang>`` compiler, if available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:180
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_VERSION_MINOR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:183
msgid ""
"Minor version of OpenMP implemented by the ``<lang>`` compiler, if available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:186
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_SPEC_DATE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:189
msgid ""
"Date of the OpenMP specification implemented by the ``<lang>`` compiler, if "
"available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:192
msgid ""
"The specification date is formatted as given in the OpenMP standard: "
"``yyyymm`` where ``yyyy`` and ``mm`` represents the year and month of the "
"OpenMP specification implemented by the ``<lang>`` compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:196
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_FLAGS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:197
msgid "OpenMP compiler flags for ``<lang>``, separated by spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:199
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_INCLUDE_DIRS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:202
msgid ""
"Directories that must be added to the header search path for ``<lang>`` when "
"using OpenMP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:205
msgid ""
"For linking with OpenMP code written in ``<lang>``, the following variables "
"are provided:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:208
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_LIB_NAMES``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:211
msgid ""
"A :ref:`semicolon-separated list <CMake Language Lists>` of OpenMP programs "
"libraries for ``<lang>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:214
msgid "``OpenMP_<libname>_LIBRARY``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:217
msgid ""
"Location of the individual libraries needed for OpenMP support in "
"``<lang>``.  The ``<libname>`` names are stored in the "
"``OpenMP_<lang>_LIB_NAMES`` list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:221
msgid "``OpenMP_<lang>_LIBRARIES``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:224
msgid ""
"A list of libraries needed to link with OpenMP code written in ``<lang>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:226
msgid "Specifically for Fortran, the module sets the following variables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:228
msgid "``OpenMP_Fortran_HAVE_OMPLIB_HEADER``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:231
msgid ""
"Boolean indicating whether OpenMP is accessible through the ``omp_lib.h`` "
"Fortran header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:234
msgid "``OpenMP_Fortran_HAVE_OMPLIB_MODULE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:237
msgid ""
"Boolean indicating whether OpenMP is accessible through the ``omp_lib`` "
"Fortran module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:240
msgid ""
"For some compilers, it may be necessary to add a header search path to find "
"the relevant OpenMP headers.  This location may be language-specific.  Where "
"this is needed, the module may attempt to find the location, but it can be "
"provided directly by setting the ``OpenMP_<lang>_INCLUDE_DIR`` cache "
"variable. Note that this variable is an *input* control to the module.  "
"Project code should use the ``OpenMP_<lang>_INCLUDE_DIRS`` *output* variable "
"if it needs to know what include directories are needed, or preferably the "
"``OpenMP::OpenMP_<lang>`` imported target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:249
msgid ""
"For Clang targeting the MSVC ABI, the module searches for the OpenMP runtime "
"library, preferring the one shipped with the compiler.  A different library "
"can be provided directly by setting the ``OpenMP_libomp_LIBRARY`` cache "
"variable.  Programs linked with it need the matching runtime DLL, such as "
"``libomp.dll``, next to them or on ``PATH`` when they run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:255
msgid ""
"In previous CMake versions, the first ``libomp`` found through the ``LIB`` "
"environment variable was used, such as the one provided with MSVC for its ``-"
"openmp:llvm`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:261
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:263
msgid ""
"Finding OpenMP support and linking the imported target to a project target "
"using the C language component:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:266
msgid ""
"find_package(OpenMP)\n"
"target_link_libraries(project_target PRIVATE OpenMP::OpenMP_C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:271
msgid "Linking a library whose ``target`` regions may be offloaded to a GPU:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:273
msgid ""
"find_package(OpenMP REQUIRED)\n"
"target_link_libraries(kernels PRIVATE OpenMP::OpenMP_CXX_Offload)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:278
msgid "and enabling offload when configuring the build, e.g. with Clang:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindOpenMP.cmake:280
msgid "$ cmake -B build -DOpenMP_CXX_OFFLOAD_FLAGS=--offload-arch=sm_80"
msgstr ""
